	(text "Firmware sequence for U12 (I²C 0x60)\n\nDrive +VARI_EN high. The chip starts at its defaults: 500 kHz, 3.5 A limit, and the output voltage set by your FB divider. That state is safe for the inductor.\nImmediately write CTL1 (0x04) bit D7 = 0. With the EN pin high, this bit takes over and turns the converter off while I²C stays alive. Use read-modify-write, not a hardcoded byte.\nWrite IOUT_LIM (0x03) = 40 (0x28). At 50 mA per LSB with a 21.5 kΩ OC resistor, that's 2.0 A. Your R55 is 21.5 kΩ, which matches.\nWrite CTL1 bits D[3:2] = 01 for 750 kHz. Keep MODE and HICCUP as they are.\nWrite VREF_L and VREF_H (0x00, 0x01), then set EN bit D7 = 1, then write GO_BIT = 1 in 0x02.\nRe-run steps 9-12 after any MCU reset. If EN is held low for more than 55 ms, the registers reset to defaults."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 423.926 153.924 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "36d5934c-7ed2-4731-98a0-d8676ecc5774")
	)
